# Titanium alloys — EcoSuit / EcoSuit-AS working list
**α · α+β · β · CP · aluminides**
Ti is not a belt-native plate metal. M-type FeNi has Ti at ppm. Treat every Ti line as Earth (or lunar ilmenite) import unless a separate oxide-reduction plant exists.

---

## 1. Families

| Family | Structure | Character | Suit job |
|---|---|---|---|
| CP (Grades 1–4) | α, unalloyed | Ductile, weldable, weaker as O rises | Lines, bellows, non-structural skins |
| α / near-α | HCP | Creep + weld, modest strength | Hot fittings, not the exo |
| α+β | HCP + BCC | The workhorses | Longerons, yoke, hatch, S1–S4 |
| β / metastable-β | BCC | Formable, high strength after STA | Springs, complex nodes, fasteners |
| TiAl / aluminides | Intermetallic | Light + hot, brittle | Not a chest plate, not a hatch seal |

