## 2. Commercially pure

| Grade | O (typ. max, order) | Strength class | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Grade 1 | lowest O | Softest CP | Max formability; bellows, COOL lines |
| Grade 2 | — | Workhorse CP | General tubing, QD bodies if loads are low |
| Grade 3 | — | Mid | Little use on the suit |
| Grade 4 | highest O of CP | Strongest CP | Still not exo structure |
| Grade 7 / 11 | +Pd | CP + crevice corrosion | Wet loops if you ever run sour analog |
| Grade 16 / 26 | +Pd lean | Same idea, cheaper Pd | — |

Do not spec Grade 1 for S1–S4. Do not spec Grade 4 as a substitute for 6Al-4V.

