## 8. Process notes that belong on the traveler

- 6-4: mill anneal for most tubes; STA only where the drawing pays for it.
- ELI: extra-low O/N/C/Fe — do not weld it with dirty CP filler and call it ELI.
- No hydrogen pickup. Pickle / vacuum / dry gas after any wet step. Ti + H = delayed cracking in a hatch ring.
- Galvanic: Ti + carbon-hemp backing + wet loop = isolate. Ti + Grade A FeNi = isolate or you eat the iron.
- Filler: ERTi-5 for 6-4; do not weld 6-4 with CP filler on a structural land.
- NDE: dye + UT on rings; conductivity is not your friend like it is on FeNi.

---

## 9. Title-block language

- Default structural Ti is Ti-6Al-4V. Write ELI when the part can kill the crew if it tears.
- CP is plumbing.
- Beta is fasteners, formed sheet, and forgings with a written STA.
- TiAl stays off the OML and off the hatch.
- Ti is an import to EcoSuit-AS. Belt plates are FeNi / superalloy. The skeleton can stay 6-4 until a reduction plant exists.